# Hooks are Node only

When you add or change a Cursor hook (`.cursor/hooks.json` plus a script under `.cursor/hooks/`), write the script in Node and invoke it with `node`. Do not use shell, Python, Deno, Bun, or any other runtime, and do not add dependencies the repo does not already have.

```json
// ❌ BAD — other runtimes
{ "command": "bash .cursor/hooks/block-secrets.sh" }
{ "command": "python3 .cursor/hooks/block_secrets.py" }
{ "command": "deno run .cursor/hooks/block-secrets.ts" }

// ✅ GOOD — Node
{ "command": "node .cursor/hooks/block-secrets-pii.mjs" }
```

- Script files are `.mjs` (or `.cjs`) so they run with the Node the repo already requires; no build step, no `ts-node`, no `npx`.
- Read the hook payload from stdin with Node built-ins (`process.stdin`, `node:fs`, `node:path`); no third-party packages.
- Every hook must run from the demo root with only `node` on the PATH.
